C  RANF.FT
      FUNCTION RANF(R)
C   RANDOM NUMBER GENERATOR
C   USES A 12-BIT MULTIPLICATIVE CONGRUENTIAL 
C   GENERATOR
C   RETURNS RANF UNIFORMLY DISTRIBUTED IN THE
C   RANGE [0.0,1.0]
C   REPEATS AFTER 512 CYCLES
	P=1845.*X1
	K=P/2048.
	X1=P-2048.*FLOAT(K)
C
	P=1963.*X2
	K=P/2048.
	X2=P-2048.*FLOAT(K)
	RANF=(X1+X2/1024.-1.)/2048.
	RETURN
C
S/   ENTRY POINT RNSET(IR)
S/   INITIALIZES RANDOM NUMBER GENERATOR
S/   CALL WITH IR AS A RANDOM INTEGER 
S	DUMMY \IR
S\IR,	BLOCK 2
S     ENTRY RNSET
SRNSET,  BLOCK 2
S     TAD I RNSET
S     DCA  \IR
S     INC  RNSET#
S     TAD I RNSET
S     DCA  \IR#
S     INC  RNSET#
S     TAD I \IR
S     AND  (3776
S     IAC        /FORCE POSITIVE, ODD
S     CALL 0,FLOT
S     CALL 1,STO
S     ARG  \X1
S/ SAME TO SET X2, USING ROTATED IR
S     TAD I \IR
S     RTL;RTL;RTL
S     AND  (3776
S     IAC
S     CALL 0,FLOT
S     CALL 1,STO
S     ARG  \X2
S     RETRN RNSET
	END
 
 
AN INDEPENDENTLY COMPUTED SET OF RANDOM NUMBERS
EXISTS ON THE FILE SYS:RANNUM.DA.   THESE NUMBERS
CAN BE USED AS SEEDS FOR THE RNSET SUBROUTINE.
 
TO RANDOMLY ADDRESS A ONE-DIMENSIONAL ARRAY OF 
LENGTH N, USE
     I=FLOAT(N)*RANF(R)+1.
IF N EXCEEDS 512, RNSET MUST BE CALLED OCCASIONALLY
TO AVOID CYCLING.
